94 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3406393675">June 23, 2020</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">You meet two royal families. King Raj commissions King Ki to bring back the daughter he knew he never knew he had by the love of his life. King ki sends his son Creston over. From the instant he sees her he knows she’s different. Creston is known for the playboy, any girl he wants he gets by smiling. When they finally meet her at her work, she’s completely ignores him which he isn’t use to. They both are attracted to each other but don’t admit to it. This relationship is beautiful as it progressively grows. When Elisha is told the truth of her father, what she thought and was told have been lies. Elisha doubts the love of her father because of impairment which Creston reassures her how much her father has loved her. <br /><br />The love between them finally get too much both having doubt they are good enough for one another but they are so perfect. Creston never knew he would ever fall in love and after being hurt so much Elisha felt the same. You go on an adventures with them. Elisha doubts that her father will love her because there are things he doesn’t know about her. Creston is always by her side supporting her, showing her how life will be. I enjoyed reading sweet prince falls in love with a princess at first time. <br /><br />I did not at one stage want to put this book down. This is the first book of Lizabeths I have read and it won’t my last. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="Rev