h="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3456930227">July 26, 2020</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Lizabeth Scott is a new to me author and I can say she has a new fan! I’ll definitely be checking out more of her work. <br />.<br />I didn’t know what to expect with this book. I’m not usually one to read blurbs so I went in blind and I can safely say I was pleasantly surprised. I usually go for the dark angsty but this was a nice change. I’m glad I gave it a go cause it’s a story that I won’t be forgetting anytime soon.<br />.<br />Amazing characters, creative and detailed world building. I enjoyed how each character was unique and who you thought was the star actually wasn’t. Lis really stood out for me. Her character presence was really pronounced even in the subtlest ways. She definitely both complimented as well as contrast nicely with Cres. Their story felt surreal but you couldn’t help but be drawn in, like a modern day fairytale.<br />.<br />Definitely a ride emotionally, not as hard hitting as what I’m accustomed too but I enjoyed this nonetheless. Definitely a well paced book. It didn’t leave you without some trying moments as well as feel good moments, it had the perfect balance of all and I’m left feeling like I experienced the best wave at the beach, excited, exhilarated and satisfied. <br />.<br />I’m definitely looking forward to what Lizabeth has in store for us next! </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span t